//==
// # Parameter-space regions of faces
//
// Layer 05-face-meshing, first half: a face as a region of its surface's natural parameter
// plane. Every UvCoordinate in this file and in uv-regions.library.plato holds NATURAL
// parameters (an angle in radians, a length in model units), not the normalized parameters the
// stdlib's comment on UvCoordinate describes.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Where a parameter-space point came from
//  - Loops and regions
//  - How a coedge reaches parameter space
//  - The chart a region is oriented and triangulated in
//  - Four-sided regions

//==
// # Where a parameter-space point came from

// The origin of one parameter-space point of a face.
//   FromVertex: the point of a model vertex. One vertex may give several points: the two copies
//     of a seam vertex, or every point of a pole segment at a pole that is a model vertex.
//   FromEdge: sample Index of the edge's EdgeDiscretization, strictly between its first and last
//     samples (1 <= Index <= count - 2); the end samples are FromVertex.
//   SeamCut: the Index-th interior point (Index >= 1) of a synthetic seam cut, on the copy of the
//     cut nearer domain side Side; the two copies of one cut carry the same Index.
//   Pole: the Index-th point of the pole segment, at a pole that is not a model vertex. The pole
//     segment lies on an iso-line the surface collapses to a point (layer 01's CollapsedAt);
//     Side is the side of the face's parameter box it runs along (VMax for a sphere's north pole,
//     VMin for a cone face above its apex, whose line lies inside the surface's domain).
//   Interior: a point RefineToSurface placed strictly inside the region.
// SeamCut and Pole points are synthetic: they are not model topology and never reach provenance
// as a vertex or an edge.
type UvPointSource
    = FromVertex(Vertex: BrepVertexIndex)
    | FromEdge(Edge: BrepEdgeIndex, Index: Integer)
    | SeamCut(Side: DomainSide, Index: Integer)
    | Pole(Side: DomainSide, Index: Integer)
    | Interior;

//==
// # Loops and regions

// One loop of a face in its surface's natural parameters: Points[i] came from Sources[i]. The
// loop runs from Points[0] to Points[Count - 1] and closes back to Points[0]; the closing point
// is not repeated. Before AddMissingSeamsAndPoles a loop may wind around a periodic direction and
// so not close in the plane; after it, every loop closes.
type UvLoop
    implements IValue
{
    Points: Array<UvCoordinate>;
    Sources: Array<UvPointSource>;
}

// A face's region in its surface's natural parameter plane: the points inside Outer and outside
// every hole. A hole of one point is a point hole (a vertex loop inside the face): it removes no
// area and is a corner of every triangulation of the region. Built by RegionOf; its invariants
// are in face-meshing.spec.plato.
type UvRegion
    implements IValue
{
    Outer: UvLoop;
    Holes: Array<UvLoop>;
}

// One parameter-space point together with its source: what LoopToUv builds a loop from.
type UvSample
    implements IValue
{
    Point: UvCoordinate;
    Source: UvPointSource;
}

//==
// # The chart a region is oriented and triangulated in

// The chart of one face: (u, v) maps to (s * ScaleU * u, ScaleV * v), with s = -1 when Mirrored
// and +1 otherwise. Mirrored is true exactly when layer 02's FaceNormalSign is -1 (the face
// normal points against PartialU x PartialV), so that du x dv in the chart maps to a positive
// multiple of the face normal at each point. ScaleU and ScaleV are
// positive: the mean speeds |PartialU| and |PartialV| over the face, so a length in the chart
// approximates a length on the surface (exact on planes and cylinders). The triangulator and the
// refinement's Delaunay decisions work in this chart; every law measures in 3D or by sign.
type FaceChart
    implements IValue
{
    Mirrored: Boolean;
    ScaleU: Number;
    ScaleV: Number;
}

//==
// # Four-sided regions

// Whether a region's outer loop is four-sided. FourSided lists the positions in Outer.Points of
// the four corners in traversal order; side k runs from corner k to corner k + 1 (modulo four).
// A side is one coedge, one seam use, one synthetic seam cut, or one pole segment (version 1).
// NotFourSided covers regions with holes, with more or fewer than four sides, and with a side
// that is not an iso-line of the natural parameters.
type QuadSides
    = NotFourSided
    | FourSided(Corners: Array<VertexIndex>);
